# Expectations for docs/outgoing/issue40-reply.md
#
# The citation gate proves a cited line EXISTS. It cannot prove the sentence
# around it is true. This file is the part that reads content: each row asserts
# that a cited line in rmtew's tree contains a given substring. Five real
# defects in this document were of exactly this class: a line cited for the
# wrong statement, a clamp described as a conditional test when it is
# unconditional, a parameter type cited at a call site instead of a
# declaration, an out-of-bounds read described as "finds nothing" when Map::At
# answers with the (0,0) square, and the same read described as silent when the
# ASSERT one line above it is what fills the error log.
#
# Format: path:line <TAB> substring that must appear on that line.

